  "transpose": false,
  "notes": "Source data for termination rates is split into two tables: one for service < 5 years (page 71) and one for service >= 5 years (page 71). The < 5 years table is by service only (no age dimension), so rates are assumed age-invariant for those service bins. The >= 5 years table is by age only (no service dimension), so rates are assumed service-invariant for those age bins. Target rows 25-65 map to printed age rows. Target row 70 has no source data (document stops at age 60 for >=5yrs service, and <5yrs service is impossible at age 70 with typical entry age). Target columns 1-4 map to service bins 1-2, 2-3, 3-4, 4-5 from the <5yrs table. Target columns 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 30, 40 map to the single '5+ Years' column from the >=5yrs table. Values are percentages in source (e.g., 12.00), but the target unit is decimal probability. The code will handle the unit conversion if 'values_unit' is set, but here we transcribe as printed. Note: The target grid asks for specific service bins (1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 30, 40). The source provides ranges (1-2, 2-3, 3-4, 4-5) and a single '5+' bucket. For the '5+' bucket, the rate is constant across all target service bins >= 5. For the <5 buckets, the rate is constant across all target ages. No overlap_weighted is used for the service bins 1-4 as the target bins (single years) are fully contained within the source bins (2-year ranges) and the source rates are assumed constant over the range. The '5+' bucket is treated as a single source for all target service columns >= 5.",
  "unavailable": false
